      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Whether internal mammary artery side branches have the potential for hemodynamically significant flow steal in cases of postcoronary surgery ischemia remains a controversial issue. We present a case in which coil embolization of two unligated side branches resulted in symptomatic improvement and resolution of ischemia as evidenced by myoview imaging.\u2003"
